From e5539a52c74a89d0c55b5a1bd94e2eb461b3842e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pieroviano <piero.viano@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 07:59:14 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Add PrinterSettings capability collections

Closes API-COMPLETENESS.md P2 item 7 (Drawing section 6): the four nested
collections PaperSizeCollection, PaperSourceCollection, PrinterResolutionCollection
and StringCollection, plus the PaperSizes/PaperSources/PrinterResolutions
properties that expose them - code enumerating a printer's capabilities did not
compile without them. Signatures (ctor(T[]), Add(T), CopyTo(T[],int),
GetEnumerator, Count, Item[int], ICollection/IEnumerable) match the net48
reference exactly, dumped via the tool's new --membersof mode.

InstalledPrinters now returns the nested PrinterSettings.StringCollection rather
than System.Collections.Specialized.StringCollection, matching WinForms. With no
print system the exposed collections are empty, consistent with the virtual-device
defaults already documented in EMULATION-GAPS.md.

Covered by PrinterSettingsCollectionsFunctionalTests (empty capability properties,
InstalledPrinters type, and the collection contract: count/indexer/enumerator/
CopyTo/Add and ICollection). Full Forms suite green at 2475.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
